   <section id="about" class="about">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">About SYNBIOCON</h2>

    <div class="about-text">
     <p>
  <strong>SYNBIOCON 2026</strong> is a first of its kind, IIT Bombay × IIT Kharagpur - led Pan-India conference focused on advancing awareness, learning, and collaboration in <strong>synthetic biology</strong> across the country. The conference brings together students, researchers, and professionals to explore how engineering principles can be applied to biological systems to address real-world challenges.
</p>

      <p>
       Through a combination of expert talks, hands-on learning, and project showcases, <strong>SYNBIOCON 2026</strong> aims to strengthen the synthetic biology ecosystem in India and provide a platform for emerging ideas, skills, and innovations to gain national visibility.
      </p>

      <div class="about-features">
        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">🎓</div>
          <h3>Expert Speaker Sessions</h3>
          <p>Engaging talks by speakers from academia, industry, and startups, offering diverse perspectives on research, innovation, and real-world applications of synthetic biology.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">🧬</div>
          <h3>Hands-on Bioinformatics Workshop</h3>
          <p>A two-day, problem-driven workshop designed to introduce bioinformatics through practical tools, guided learning, and real biological datasets.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature">
          <div class="feature-icon">🏆</div>
          <h3>iGEM Project Showcase</h3>
          <p>Presentations by finalist and winning iGEM teams, highlighting impactful synthetic biology projects, design approaches, and translational potential.</p>
        </div>
        </div>  </div>  </div>  </section>
  
